%% Diagram: Snowpipe auto-ingest architecture (sequence)
%% Source lecture: Snowflake Complete Masterclass - Section 11 (Snowpipe)
%% Description:  S3 object_created event → SQS (via notification integration)
%%               → Snowflake-managed serverless pipe → target table.
%%               The pipe runs COPY INTO every ~1 minute; no warehouse billed.
%% Author: Prem Vishnoi <pvishnoi@avilx.com>
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor Producer
    participant S3 as S3 Bucket
    participant SQS as SQS Queue<br/>(notification integration)
    participant SP  as Snowpipe (serverless)
    participant TBL as Target Table

    Producer->>S3: PUT new file orders_2026_10_10.csv
    S3-->>SQS: S3 Event Notification<br/>s3:ObjectCreated:*
    SQS-->>SP: ReceiveMessage<br/>(auto-poll by Snowflake)
    SP->>S3: GET file (via storage integration)
    S3-->>SP: file bytes
    SP->>TBL: COPY INTO<br/>(auto, ~1 min latency)
    SP-->>SQS: DeleteMessage
```
